## 5. Encryption Architecture

### 5.1 Protocol Choice
**Signal Protocol** (Extended Diffie-Hellman + Double Ratchet Algorithm)
- Industry standard used by WhatsApp, Signal, Wire
- Provides Perfect Forward Secrecy (PFS)
- Post-Compromise Security

### 5.2 Key Hierarchy

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        KEY HIERARCHY                             │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                  │
│  Identity Key Pair (IK)          ← Long-term, per device        │
│       │                                                          │
│  Signed Pre-Key (SPK)            ← Medium-term (weekly rotate)  │
│       │                                                          │
│  One-Time Pre-Keys (OPK)         ← Single use, 100 pre-loaded   │
│       │                                                          │
│  Session Keys (Double Ratchet)   ← Per message, forward secure  │
│                                                                  │
│  Group Sender Key                ← Per group, per device        │
│  Media Encryption Key            ← Per file, AES-256-GCM        │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 5.3 1-to-1 Message Encryption Flow

```
Sender A                    Server                    Receiver B
    │                          │                          │
    │ 1. Fetch B's key bundle  │                          │
    │─────────────────────────►│                          │
    │◄─────────────────────────│                          │
    │ (IK_B, SPK_B, OPK_B)    │                          │
    │                          │                          │
    │ 2. X3DH Key Agreement    │                          │
    │ (local computation)      │                          │
    │                          │                          │
    │ 3. Derive Session Key    │                          │
    │ 4. Encrypt message       │                          │
    │    (AES-256-GCM)         │                          │
    │                          │                          │
    │ 5. Send encrypted blob   │                          │
    │─────────────────────────►│                          │
    │                          │ 6. Store & forward       │
    │                          │─────────────────────────►│
    │                          │                          │
    │                          │           7. B decrypts  │
    │                          │           (local key)    │
```

### 5.4 Group Encryption (Sender Keys)

```
Group Creation:
1. Group admin generates group key pair
2. Each member generates a SenderKey
3. SenderKeys distributed to all members via encrypted 1-to-1 channels
4. Messages encrypted with sender's SenderKey
5. All members can decrypt (they have all SenderKeys)

Member Addition:
- New member receives all existing SenderKeys via encrypted channel
- Optional: Key rotation on member add (configurable)

Member Removal:
- Mandatory SenderKey rotation for all remaining members
- Ensures forward secrecy after member removal
```

### 5.5 Media Encryption

```
Upload Flow:
1. Client generates random AES-256-GCM key + IV
2. File encrypted locally (client-side)
3. Encrypted blob uploaded to Storage Service
4. Encrypted media key shared with recipient(s) via E2E encrypted message
5. CDN serves only encrypted blobs

Download Flow:
1. Client receives encrypted media key from message
2. Client downloads encrypted blob from CDN
3. Client decrypts blob locally
4. Media rendered in-app only
```

### 5.6 Key Rotation Policy

| Key Type | Rotation Interval | Trigger |
|----------|------------------|---------|
| Identity Key | Never (device lifetime) | Device replacement |
| Signed Pre-Key | Weekly | Time-based |
| One-Time Pre-Keys | Per use | Consumption |
| Group Sender Key | Member remove + weekly | Event + time-based |
| Session Ratchet | Per message | Automatic |

