### 6.3 Database Sharding Strategy

**Sharding Key**: `user_id` (consistent hashing)

| Data Type | Strategy | Rationale |
|-----------|---------|-----------|
| Users, Profiles | Single shard (user_id) | Low volume, high access |
| Messages | Sharded by chat_id | Hotspot prevention |
| Media metadata | Sharded by user_id | Co-located with user |
| Events/Analytics | Time-partitioned | Efficient range scans |

### 6.4 Redis Architecture

```
Redis Cluster (6 nodes: 3 primary + 3 replica)

Usage:
├── Session Store (TTL-based)
├── JWT Blacklist (token revocation)
├── Rate Limiting (sliding window counters)
