## 9. Voice & Video Strategy

### 9.1 WebRTC Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    WebRTC Infrastructure                      │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                              │
│  Signaling: WebSocket (Socket.IO)                           │
│  ICE Gathering: STUN + TURN                                 │
│                                                              │
│  1-to-1 Calls: Peer-to-Peer (P2P) preferred                 │
│  Group Calls: SFU (Selective Forwarding Unit)               │
│               → mediasoup 3.x                               │
│                                                              │
│  STUN Server: coturn (self-hosted) + Google STUN fallback   │
│  TURN Server: coturn (self-hosted, multi-region)            │
│                                                              │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 9.2 1-to-1 Call Flow

```
Caller (A)          Signaling Server          Callee (B)
   │                       │                      │
   │── call:initiate ──────►│                      │
   │                       │── call:incoming ─────►│
   │                       │                      │
   │◄──────────────────── call:ringing ────────────│
   │                       │                      │
   │                       │◄──── call:accept ─────│
   │◄──────────── call:accepted ───────────────────│
   │                       │                      │
   │── ICE candidates ─────►│──── ICE candidates ──►│
   │◄──── ICE candidates ───│◄─── ICE candidates ───│
   │                       │                      │
   │◄══════════ P2P Media Stream (Encrypted) ══════│
```

### 9.3 Group Call Architecture (SFU)

```
Participant A ──► SFU (mediasoup) ──► Participant B
Participant C ──► SFU (mediasoup) ──► Participant C
Participant B ──► SFU (mediasoup) ──► Participant A

- SFU receives streams from each participant
- Selectively forwards streams to each subscriber
- Supports up to 200 participants per group call
- Adaptive bitrate per subscriber connection quality
```

### 9.4 Voice Quality Features

| Feature | Implementation |
|---------|---------------|
| Noise Suppression | WebRTC built-in + RNNoise |
| Echo Cancellation | WebRTC AEC built-in |
| Adaptive Bitrate | WebRTC built-in GCC |
| Bandwidth Estimation | WebRTC REMB/TWCC |
| Codec | Opus (audio), VP8/VP9/H.264 (video) |

### 9.5 Call Recording Architecture

```
Recording is server-side (mediasoup → GStreamer → S3)
1. On recording start: mediasoup pipes streams to GStreamer
2. GStreamer encodes to MP4 (H.264 + AAC)
3. Chunks uploaded to encrypted S3 bucket
4. Post-call: Final MP4 assembled and stored
5. Recording URL delivered to participants
```

### 9.6 TURN Server Infrastructure

| Region | Servers | Protocol |
|--------|---------|---------|
| US-East | 2x coturn | UDP/TCP/TLS |
| EU-West | 2x coturn | UDP/TCP/TLS |
| AP-South | 2x coturn | UDP/TCP/TLS |

