## 10. Media System Strategy

### 10.1 Supported Media Types

| Type | Max Size | Processing |
|------|----------|-----------|
| Images | 25 MB | Resize, thumbnail, WebP conversion |
| Videos | 2 GB | Transcode (HLS), thumbnail |
| Audio | 100 MB | Normalize, waveform generation |
| Documents | 500 MB | Virus scan, preview generation |
| Voice Notes | 25 MB | Waveform generation |

### 10.2 Chunked Upload Architecture

```
Client                        Media Service              Storage
  │                                │                       │
  │ POST /media/upload/init        │                       │
  │ {file_size, mime, chunk_count} │                       │
  │──────────────────────────────►│                       │
  │◄────────── {upload_id} ────────│                       │
  │                                │                       │
  │ PUT /media/upload/{id}/chunk/1 │                       │
  │──────────────────────────────►│──────── S3 multipart ─►│
  │◄─────── {chunk_ack} ───────────│◄─────────────────────│
  │                                │                       │
  │ PUT /media/upload/{id}/chunk/N │                       │
  │──────────────────────────────►│──────── S3 multipart ─►│
  │                                │                       │
  │ POST /media/upload/{id}/complete│                      │
  │──────────────────────────────►│─── S3 complete ───────►│
  │◄──────── {media_url} ──────────│                       │
```

### 10.3 Media Processing Pipeline

```
Upload Complete
      │
      ▼
Virus Scan (ClamAV) ──FAIL──► Quarantine + Alert
      │ PASS
      ▼
MIME Validation ──FAIL──► Reject
      │ PASS
      ▼
Encrypt (AES-256-GCM) ──► Encrypted Blob → S3
      │
      ▼
Generate Thumbnail
      │
      ▼
Transcode (if video) → HLS segments → S3
      │
      ▼
Update media_files record
      │
      ▼
Return CDN URL (signed, TTL)
```

### 10.4 CDN Architecture

```
Storage (MinIO/S3)
       │
       ▼
CDN Origin (CloudFront / custom Nginx)
       │
       ▼
Edge Nodes (Global PoPs)
       │
       ▼
Client (signed URL, TTL=1hr)
```

